$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General protocol: To a stirred solution of the
primary alcohol (0.2 mmol) in dichloromethane (0.4 mL, 0.5 M) at room
temperature under argon was added successively the tetraethylammonium
halide (0.3 mmol) and 2,6-lutidine (69 μL, 0.6 mmol). XtalFluor-E (69 mg,
0.3 mmol) was then added and the solution was stirred for 18 h at the
same temperature. The reaction mixture was quenched by aqueous sodium
carbonate (5%) and the aqueous phase was extracted with dichloromethane
(3X). The combined organic extracts were washed with 10% HCl (1X), water
(1X) and brine (1X). Then, the resulting mixture was dried over anhydrous
MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The crude material was
purified with flash chromatography to give the desired product.
3-(Chloromethyl)phenol (3l) Following the general method on a 0.5 mmol
scale of 3-hydroxybenzyl alcohol (1l) using tetraethylammonium chloride,
the desired product (50 mg, 70%) was isolated as a yellow oil by flash
chromatography using ethyl acetate/hexane (30:70). IR (ATR, ZnSe) ν =
3352, 1589, 1455, 1278, 1255, 1156, 783, 746 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.23 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 6.96 (m, 1H), 6.88 (m, 1H), 6.79 (ddd,
J = 8.1, 2.6, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 4.84 (s, 2H), 4.54 (s, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 155.8, 139.3, 130.1, 121.1, 115.6, 46.1; HRMS-ESI calcd for
C7H6ClO [M-H]- 141.0113, found 141.0118.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogenation of Primary Alcohols Using a Tetraethylammonium
Halide/[Et2NSF2]BF4 Combination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
