$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Diluted Chlorination
Reactions. To an ice-cold 1.0 M solution of alcohol in dichloromethane
was added thionyl chloride (1.5 equiv) and stirred for 1 h. Hydrogen
chloride which is generated during this step was vented from the
reaction. The reaction mixture was then diluted to the required
concentration (usually 0.5 or 0.01 M) by adding the required amount
dichloromethane via syringe and cooled to the required temperature
(usually −78 or 0 °C). After 1 h, TiCl4 was added (catalytic to
stoichiometric amounts) and stirred for the required time. The reaction
mixture was quenched with water, stirred until both layers were clear,
and extracted three times with dichloromethane. The collected organic
extracts were concentrated and the resulting oil was purified by silica
gel chromatography (usually using pure hexanes as eluent). yieldb (%) 70,
(1S, 3R)-1-chloro-3-methylcyclohexane (racemic) (1S,
3R)-1-chloro-3-methylcyclohexane (racemic): 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
3.88−3.80 (tt, J = 11.69, 4.14 Hz, 1H), 2.19−2.14 (m, 2H), 1.82−1.75 (m,
1H), 1.66−1.61 (m, 1H),1.53−1.41 (m, 2H), 1.33−1.21 (m, 2H), 0.92 (d, J =
6.54 Hz, 3H), 0.90−0.80 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 59.7, 45.9,
36.9, 33.5, 33.1, 25.9, 22.2. Known compound.38
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 2 eq. of titanium tetrachloride used, incremental
addition (DCM stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereoretentive Chlorination of Cyclic Alcohols Catalyzed by Titanium(IV)
Tetrachloride: Evidence for a Front Side Attack Mechanism
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mondal, Deboprosad; Li, Song Ye; Bellucci, Luca; Laino, Teodoro; Tafi,
Andrea; Guccione, Salvatore; Lepore, Salvatore D.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2013), 78(5), 2118-2127

