$DATUM 67-64-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reaction of 4-iodo-2-methylphenoxyacetic acid with triethanolamine.
Freshly distilled triethanolamine was added to 5.84 g (20 mmol) of
4-iodo-2-methylphenoxyacetic acid in 35 mL of anhydrous acetone, and the
mixture was heated for 5-6 h under reflux. The mixture was cooled, and
the precipitate was filtered off and washed with diethyl ether.
2-Iodoethyl(bis-2-hydroxyethyl)amine. Yield 3.92 g (76%), colorless
crystals. 4-Hydroxy-2-methylphenoxyacetic acid was isolated by removal of
the solvent from the filtrate. 3.51 g (96%), viscous grease-like
material. 2-Iodoethyl(bis-2-hydroxyethyl)amine; Mp 157°C. IR spectrum, ν,
cm-1: 3354 (O-H), 1338 (δ O-H), 1229, 1126 (C-N), 1051 (C-O), 439 (C-I).
Found, %: C 27.38; H 5.56; I 48.93; N 5.43. C6H14INO2. Calculated, %: C
27.82; H 5.45; I 48.98; N 5.40. 4-Hydroxy-2-methylphenoxyacetic acid; IR
spectrum, ν, cm-1: 3353 (O-H), 3108 (O-H), 1774 (C=O), 1229 (δ O-H), 1051
(C-O). Found, %: C 58.53; H 5.52. C9H11O4. Calculated, %: C 59.33; H
5.53.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Tris(2-hydroxyethyl)ammonium 4-halo-2-methylphenoxyacetates
(halocresacins)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
