synthesis of allyl chlorides from Baylis-Hillman adducts (1a-v) To a
stirred solution of triphosgene (0.93 g, 3.14 mmol) in dichloromethane
(5mL) at 0°C, pyridine (1.26mL, 15.72 mmol) was added drop-wise followed
by Baylis-Hillman adduct (1m) (0.5 g, 3.14 mmol) in DCM (5 mL) and
stirred the reaction at room temperature (Monitored by TLC). After
completion of the reaction, the reaction mixture was diluted with DCM (10
mL); the organic layer was washed with water (5mL), sat. CuSO4 solution
(5mL), dried over Na2SO4 and the solvent was removed under reduced
pressure to get the desired allyl chloride (2m). Same experimental
procedure was adopted for the preparation of other allyl chlorides. 2.2q
