$DATUM PCl5 System. To a solution of alcohols 1f (1.0 mmol) and 13 (1.0 mmol) in
dry CCl4 (1 mL) was added PCl5 (0.5 mmol) at 77 °C for 30 min. Aqueous
NaHCO3 (15%, 10mL) was added to the reaction mixture. The mixture was
extracted with diethyl ether. The organic layer was washed with water and
dried over MgSO4. The volatiles were evaporated under reduced pressure,
and the residue showed the formation of 14 (73%) and 3f (15%). The
recovery of 1f (ca. 80%) was observed. Compound 14, yield (73%), Compound
3f, yield (15%)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
