$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-Chloromethyl-pyrrolidine-1-carboxylic acid
tert-butyl ester: 2,4,6-Trichloro-[1,3,5]-triazine (1.83 g, 10.0 mmol)
was added to DMF (2 mL), maintained at 25 °C. After the formation of a
white solid, CH2Cl2 (25 mL) was added, followed by NaHCO3 (3.19 g, 38.0
mmol) and successively by N-Boc-prolinol (1.91 g, 9.5 mmol). After the
addition, the mixture was stirred at room temperature, monitored (TLC)
until completion (40 min). Water (20 mL) was added then the organic phase
washed with 15 mL of a saturated solution of Na2CO3, followed by 1 N HCl
and brine. The organic layer were dried (Na2SO4) and the solvent
evaporated. 2-chloromethyl-pyrrolidine-1-carboxylic acid tert-butyl
ester(entry 7) yield: 94% entry 8 yield: 70 b %
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An Efficient Route to Alkyl Chlorides from Alcohols Using the Complex
TCT/DMF
